{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And I shall lie with my fathers.</b> The matter of a deceased person's lying with his fathers is the resting of the deceased's bed in the place of mourning, surrounded by the mourners. Therefore this expression is written of all the kings, righteous and wicked alike, who died upon their beds in the book of Kings." "<b>And you shall carry me out of Egypt.</b> And when you act in this manner you will be able to carry me out of Egypt, for when the days of mourning are fulfilled my grief will have departed from their hearts, as in וַיַּעַבְרוּ יְמֵי בְכִיתוֹ (Genesis 50:4), and they will not object to your carrying me to another land." "<b>I will do as you have said.</b> I, for my own part, will do as you have said with all my strength."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:04.100324698Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}